Executable Specification Guide
===============================================================================

This documentation profile explains the reflective conformance prototype. A
release render is generated from a pinned determinism bundle. Documentation is
parsed by the unified Mech frontend but is not permitted to mutate the runtime
under test.

specification-profile := "mspec"
bundle-policy := "content-addressed"

Using the prototype
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Run mech spec check to collect fresh v0.4 resident-executor evidence and write
the console, JSON, and HTML conformance views. Run mech spec record to add the
same result and its source inputs to the content-addressed evidence store. The
printed bundle hash can then be passed to mech spec replay.

Run mech spec demo to inject semantic, repository-architecture, backend
admission, and broken-document-reference faults. The demonstration succeeds
only when every bad change is detected and the failed semantic witness replays
identically.

Prototype boundary
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The current vertical slice observes resident turns, a missing hard activation
grant, rejected-instance cleanup, explicit transaction commit and abort,
shutdown, repository dependency edges, benchmark protocol identity, and
explicit GPU unavailability. A real GPU numerical differential observer
remains follow-on work. The report does not call that unimplemented check a
pass.
